%description:

Tcp.fastopenClientNoCookieRequired:on -- the SYN carries the data without a cookie and without a Fast Open option.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "TCP Fast Open, client: send the data on the SYN without a cookie and without a
Fast Open option (Linux tcp_fastopen bit 0x4), for a server that accepts it; RFC 7413 requires a
cookie".

The classes: off (false, the default), on (true), and changed (the parameter is @mutable). The
code: with true, TcpConnection::process_OPEN_ACTIVE() lets the SYN wait for the first SEND also
without a cookie, and TcpConnection::writeHeaderOptions() puts no Fast Open option on it. This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host1, a Fast Open client (precondition), without a cookie of host2; host2 is a
Fast Open server that takes data without a cookie (preconditions). host1 opens a connection with
Fast Open and sends 500 bytes. Observation: level 1, the SYN of host1 carries 500 bytes and no Fast Open option.

%# parameter: Tcp.fastopenClientNoCookieRequired
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.fastopenClientNoCookieRequired
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpFastopenClientNoCookieRequiredOn")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); app.sendData(app.socket(), 500); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 1 with Fast Open, and sends 500 bytes"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie == "-" && matchesExpression(context.event.packet, "pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength");
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 1: 500 bytes, no Fast Open option")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpFastopenClientNoCookieRequiredOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientNoCookieRequired = true    # the parameter under test
*.host2.tcp.fastopenServerEnabled = true
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true
*.host2.tcp.fastopenAcceptWithoutCookie = true
*.host1.numApps = 2
*.host1.app[*].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpFastopenClientNoCookieRequiredOn: PASS
